{
  "_readme": "AI Signal source registry (Editorial Engine v1, approved 28 Sep 2026). tier 1 = primary, can be sole evidence. tier 2 = secondary, trace to the original where possible. tier 3 = discovery only, never sole evidence. 'feed' is the RSS/Atom URL; null means no feed (manual source). 'feed_verified' is true only for feeds proven by a successful pipeline run. Every run writes a feed health report into the day's data file: fix or remove feeds that keep failing. image_policy decides whether the Visual Agent may show the source's own image: 'press' (newsroom/press kit, preferred), 'official_with_credit' (the company's own blog image about its own product, shown with a visible credit and link), 'never' (publications and research whose images are licensed or unclear: Getty/AP/Reuters photos, third-party figures). When in doubt, use 'never'. This is an editorial policy, not legal advice. image_hosts lists extra domains where a source serves its own images (e.g. its CDN). The daily pull request tells you which host to add when a genuine company image was rejected.",
